# Design system reuse

Before adding or changing UI, read [frontend/DESIGN.md](frontend/DESIGN.md) and [frontend/src/app/globals.css](frontend/src/app/globals.css).

## Rules

1. **Prefer shared components** — `src/components/ui/`, `src/components/klassenpilot/`, `src/components/assistant-ui/` (registry). Import and compose; do not reinvent controls inline on pages.
2. **No one-off styling** — Do not duplicate Tailwind class strings for the same control across files. If a pattern may appear twice or is domain-wide (segmented toggles, toolbars, cards), add or extend a component in `ui/` first, then consume it.
3. **Semantic tokens only** — Use `bg-accent`, `bg-muted`, `text-primary`, `border-border`, etc. No ad-hoc hex in feature code.
4. **Green is scarce** — `Button variant="default"` (solid primary) only for the main CTA per action group (e.g. save, chat send). Secondary controls use `outline`, `ghost`, or `SegmentedToggle`.
5. **Exception** — Customize styling in a single place only when the user explicitly asks for a one-off or page-specific exception.

## Examples

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Edit / Preview (or similar modes) | `SegmentedToggle` from `@/components/ui/segmented-toggle` |
| Highlight panel / callout | `Card variant="highlight"` |
| Equal-weight workflow destinations | `Button` / `ActionLink` `variant="soft"` |
| Dismissible amber help / sticky note | `StickyNote` from `@/components/ui/sticky-note` |
| Primary action | `Button variant="default"` once per row |
